---
description: UI and layout changes must also work on mobile, not only desktop.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Mobile is part of the change

When you add or change UI, layout, styling, or interaction, **include the mobile layout in the same change**. Do not ship a desktop-only version and wait to be asked to fix phones.

This app’s builder is a narrow column on small screens (stacked nav, `pb-24` for the preview button, `md:` at 768px). Assume a ~320–390px viewport.

## Do

- Stack or reflow at `md` (or `sm`) instead of squeezing two/three desktop columns onto a phone.
- Keep the same behavior: if a control exists on desktop (checkbox, date, skip, tour), decide its mobile placement in the same PR — beside, below, or intentionally hidden (e.g. tour targets that are `hidden md:flex`).
- Avoid `min-width` / fixed widths that overflow; use `w-full min-w-0` below `md`, and floor widths only from `md` up.
- Watch card chrome (`pr-16` for Remove, padding) so fields are not clipped under buttons.
- Prefer one component with responsive classes over a desktop-only implementation.

## Don’t

```tsx
// BAD: Present sits in the end-date column and min-width clips on phones
<div className="grid grid-cols-2">
  <input type="month" className="min-w-[14rem]" />
  <input type="month" className="min-w-[14rem]" />
</div>
```

```tsx
// GOOD: full-width stack on mobile, equal columns + extra slot from md
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:col-span-2 md:grid-cols-[minmax(14rem,1fr)_minmax(14rem,1fr)_auto]">
  <input type="month" className="w-full min-w-0 md:min-w-[14rem]" />
  <input type="month" className="w-full min-w-0 md:min-w-[14rem]" />
</div>
```

If a change cannot reasonably work on mobile, say so and hide or replace it at that breakpoint in the same edit.
